    "result_text": "All done. The build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Consolidated duplicate detection into one derived `identityKey`.**\n\nThe key is `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, and a create is rejected with 409 only when a request's *whole* key equals an existing owner's.\n\nNew code:\n- **`OwnerIdentity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a small public helper that formats the key from its three canonical components (E.164 telephone, lower-cased email, household id), reusing the existing `OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerEmail` normalizers. Single responsibility: key derivation.\n- **`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`** \u2014 the one pipeline step that replaces the three old checks. It derives the request's key (its would-be household id comes from `Household.id(...)` only when `sharesHousehold=true`, mirroring `AssignOwnerHousehold`) and compares it against every existing owner's key.\n- **`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`** + handler + escalation YAML \u2192 409 Conflict, carrying the offending `identityKey`.\n\nRemoved (folded into the above): `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone/Email/Household`, the three `DuplicateOwner*Exception` classes + handlers, and their escalation YAMLs. The POST pipeline now has a single `unique:` step \u2192 `cityCapacity`.\n\n**Behaviour change, as specified:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The test's case \u2014 same telephone, no email, no shared household for either \u2192 identical `+61\u2026||` keys \u2192 409.\n\n**Returning `identityKey`:** added it as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (regenerates into `OwnerDto`) and mapped it in `OwnerMapper` via `identityKey(owner)`, alongside the other derived fields.",
